---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';
import { BOOK, PUBLISHER, SITE } from '../config/site';

/**
 * Terms of use and of sale, written from what the app and the order flow do
 * today (Stripe takes the card, Gelato prints, every order is confirmed by
 * hand). A draft for the same lawyer who reviews the privacy policy: the
 * points to check are the remedy for damaged or misprinted books, the
 * liability section and which law governs, which this draft leaves out.
 */
const UPDATED = 'October 9, 2026';
const EMAIL = SITE.supportEmail;

const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms', path: '/terms/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use and Sale | BabyBookAI"
  description="The terms for using the BabyBookAI app and ordering a printed baby photo book: your photos, orders and payment, printing and delivery, and damaged books."
  schema={[breadcrumbs(trail)]}
  cta="terms"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={trail} />

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-20 pt-8">
    <p class="font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal">Terms</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-[2.6rem] text-teal sm:text-6xl">Terms of use and sale</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-ink-soft">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-card border-2 border-hair bg-surface p-6 sm:p-10">
      <p class="text-lg">
        These terms apply to the {SITE.name} app and to the printed books ordered through it. {SITE.name} is a
        {' '}{PUBLISHER.name} product (“we”, “us”). By using the app or ordering a book you agree to them. Questions:{' '}
        <a class="text-teal underline" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">The app</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        The app is free to download and use. Making a book and looking through it costs nothing; you pay only if you
        order a printed book. You may use the app for your own personal, non-commercial use. We may improve, change or
        stop features of the app over time.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Your photos and words</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Your photos and your words remain yours. We claim no rights over them.</li>
        <li>
          When you order, you allow us and our printer to use the book file only to print, ship and support that
          order, as the <a class="text-teal underline" href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> describes.
        </li>
        <li>
          You confirm that you have the right to print the photos and words in your book, and that nothing in it is
          unlawful. We may decline to print a book that is.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Orders and payment</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>You must be 18 or older to place an order.</li>
        <li>
          The app shows the full price before you pay, in US dollars, with shipping included. A {BOOK.pagesMin}-page
          book is ${BOOK.priceUsd}; extra pages, up to {BOOK.pagesMax}, cost more and are priced in the app.
        </li>
        <li>Payment is taken by card through Stripe. We never see your card details.</li>
        <li>
          We check every order before it goes to print. If we cannot fulfil an order, we cancel it and refund you in
          full.
        </li>
        <li>
          Before you pay, look through the whole book: photos, names, dates and spelling. Each book is printed exactly
          as you approve it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Printing and delivery</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Books are printed on demand by our print partner and shipped to the address you give. Delivery times shown are
        estimates. Please check the address carefully: we cannot redirect a book once it has shipped.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Damaged, misprinted or lost books</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        Every book is made for you, so we cannot take it back if you change your mind. If your book arrives damaged,
        has a printing defect, or does not arrive, write to{' '}
        <a class="text-teal underline" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> within 30 days of delivery (or of the
        expected delivery date) with your order email and, if you can, a photo. We will reprint the book or refund
        you. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under the consumer law where you live.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Liability</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We work hard to make the app and the books right, but the app is provided as it is. To the extent the law
        allows, our liability for an order is limited to what you paid for it. We are not responsible for photos lost
        on your phone: the app reads your photos but never deletes them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl text-teal">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">
        We may update these terms. Changes are posted here with a new date, and apply to orders placed after that date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
